{"name":"Pasilla Chiles","hex":"#44413b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pasilla","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of chili (a dried chilaca), used especially in sauces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pasilla"},{"term":"chiles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of chile"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chiles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pasilla","blocks":[{"text":"The pasilla chile or chile negro is the dried form of the chilaca chili pepper, a long and narrow member of the species Capsicum annuum. Named for its dark, wrinkled skin, it is a mild to hot, rich-flavored chile. As dried, it is generally 6 to 8 inches long and 1 to 1+1⁄2 inches in diameter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Pasillachiles.jpg/330px-Pasillachiles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pasilla","wikidata":"Q838835"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Fresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg/500px-Fresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Fresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg/1280px-Fresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Fresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg/500px-Fresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh dark brown chilaca peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFresh_chilaca_chillies.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/PasillaKnife.jpg/500px-PasillaKnife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/PasillaKnife.jpg/1280px-PasillaKnife